{"term":"retire","senses":[{"id":"kaikki:033b79435f00ab0877","definition":"To stop working on a permanent basis, usually because of old age or illness.","example":"Having made a large fortune, he retired.","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"intransitive","wordFamily":["retire hurt","retirable","retiral","retirant","retiree","retirer","retire the side","unretire"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/retire#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:0c3a5dfed9a6c318d9","definition":"To stop playing their sport and in competitions a sports player.","example":"I have decided to retire from football at the end of the season after the World Cup.","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"intransitive","wordFamily":["retire hurt","retirable","retiral","retirant","retiree","retirer","retire the side","unretire"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/retire#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:bf455eb6ebaa90af03","definition":"To withdraw; to take away.","example":"He […] retired himself, his wife, and children into a forest.","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"reflexive, sometimes","register":"reflexive, sometimes, transitive","wordFamily":["retire hurt","retirable","retiral","retirant","retiree","retirer","retire the side","unretire"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/retire#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:dc495a9d2a6a09a93a","definition":"To cease use or production of something.","example":"The steamship made thousands of trips over several decades before it was retired by the shipping company.","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],